        <mxCell id="key_note" value="Trial arrangement; long-term options A (own account) or B (own EKS) keep this design." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontColor=#AAAAAA;fontSize=9;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1530" y="568" width="265" height="28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ================= LEGEND ================= -->
        <mxCell id="legend" value="What the numbers mean" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#FF9900;fontColor=#FF9900;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="1280" width="1780" height="420" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend_txt" value="① &lt;b&gt;SWIFT ingress.&lt;/b&gt; SWIFT reaches an internal NLB in the lb subnets over SIPN. The NLB passes TCP straight through to the RPC pods (IP targets, registered by the load-balancer controller's TargetGroupBinding). mTLS, method scoping and the account allowlist are enforced by Besu itself. No public endpoint anywhere. Internal applications use a second internal NLB (JWT-authenticated).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;② &lt;b&gt;The ledger.&lt;/b&gt; Four QBFT validators (keeps running with 1 down, stops with 2 down) on a dedicated, tainted node group in ledger subnets, one validator per node (required anti-affinity), spread across all three AZs. PodDisruptionBudget maxUnavailable 0 and OnDelete updates mean neither a drain nor a Helm upgrade can take two at once. Node rotation follows the written agreement: never forced, one node at a time. Default-deny NetworkPolicy, enforced by the CNI, keeps every other pod away from them.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;③ &lt;b&gt;Air-gapped.&lt;/b&gt; No IGW, NAT or default route. Every AWS call goes through an interface endpoint with Private DNS; image layers and Terraform state go through the S3 gateway endpoint. A missing endpoint hangs rather than errors, so it is checked before every deployment. Subnet rules must allow flows F-1 to F-10 (ours) and C-1 to C-4 (the cluster's); NACLs separate roles, while security groups and NetworkPolicy protect services.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;④ &lt;b&gt;Keys.&lt;/b&gt; Each pod has its own IAM role (IRSA, trust limited by sub + aud to our namespace's service account) and reads only its own secrets, encrypted with our KMS key. Every decrypt is in CloudTrail. The node role has no access to our data, and IMDSv2 hop limit 1 keeps pods off the node role.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;⑤ &lt;b&gt;Deployment.&lt;/b&gt; GitHub Actions mirrors images into ECR by digest and publishes a versioned package to Octopus Cloud; it never deploys. Octopus applies the AWS-API Terraform from a hosted worker, and runs the in-cluster layer and the one-validator-at-a-time rolling script on the In-VPC EC2 Runner. The runner's Tentacle polls out through the cloud team's shared egress proxy: runner /32 only, two hostnames, port 443, no TLS inspection, specific-prefix route over the Transit Gateway. Nothing inbound.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;⑥ &lt;b&gt;Operator access.&lt;/b&gt; Session Manager to the runner only (no SSH, no bastion, no public IP); kubectl port-forward from there for Blockscout and the admin RPC listener, which is never behind a load balancer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;⑦ &lt;b&gt;Observability.&lt;/b&gt; Metrics and logs go to CloudWatch; alarms go to operators through SNS. Key alarms: a validator out of the producing set for more than 5 minutes, blocks stalled, pod sandbox failures (address exhaustion), unhealthy NLB targets.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;⑧ &lt;b&gt;Event pipeline (planned, purple).&lt;/b&gt; A tailer in the besu-app namespace reads contract events (eth_getLogs, durable cursor) → SNS FIFO → SQS FIFO → consumers → bank systems, deleting a message only after the receiver's durable acknowledgement; archived to S3. No Lambda anywhere." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontColor=#E6E6E6;fontSize=11;spacingLeft=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1310" width="1760" height="385" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
